course: dictionary
lesson: 3659
title: Fisher and fishers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A fisher is someone who catches fish, either as a job or for fun. A fisherman or a fisherwoman is a fisher too. «Jesus called fishermen such as Peter, Andrew, James and John» tells you that fishermen are the same kind of people as fishers.
explain: The word fisher can also mean an animal that catches fish, such as a kingfisher. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning is right. If the sentence talks about people, fisher means a person. If the sentence talks about birds or otters, it means an animal.
explain: «Vikings were Norse people from Denmark, Norway and Sweden, and most Norse people were farmers, fishers and traders.» Farmers and traders are people who work, so fishers must be people who work too. Fishers are people who catch fish, and the clue is in the list.
fact: A fisher is a person who catches fish.
fact: Fishers can be men or women, so fisherman and fisherwoman both mean a fisher.
fact: A kingfisher is a bird that catches fish, and it is an animal, not a person.
fact: The plural of fisher is fishers, meaning more than one fisher.
fact: The Bible tells how Jesus called fishers to follow him, and in the story he called them «fishers of people».
exercise: In «Jesus called fishermen such as Peter, Andrew, James and John», who were the fishermen? | *Fishers | Teachers from the town | Kings and queens | Farmers who grew corn
exercise: A kingfisher is a bird that catches fish. What does the word fisher mean in kingfisher? | *Something that catches fish | A bird that sings at night | A king who likes fishing | A small boat
exercise: Which word is the plural of fisher? | *fishers | fish | fishes | fisherer
test: In «most Norse people were farmers, fishers and traders», what are fishers? | Helmets worn in battle | Kings of the sea | *People who catch fish | Boats that carry people across the sea
test: The word fisher includes both men and women who fish. Which two people are fishers? | Only children | Only men | *A man who fishes and a woman who fishes | Only animals
exam: A North American forest animal like a large weasel is also called a... | kingfisher | fishmonger | fishbowl | *fisher cat
